GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC9 §4): the wide picture's side strips continue the screen's 2D
effects from its edges.

- GPU2D_Soft: in a strip's pass each window takes the line's window state at the screen's edge
  beside it (a wipe or an iris covers the strip once it reaches that edge), where 0001 had the
  strips outside every window. A 256-pixel-wide text background that's a fill (each line it
  shows at both edges is one colour over 8 pixels there, this frame and the last: a battle's
  closing squares, a wipe) continues as that colour, over the 3D scene only; other 256-wide
  layers stay out of the strips (a text box, a banner at one edge, a picture, a patterned panel).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

